<HelloFraandsPage updated="2026-10-14" title="Influencer agreement" summary="Influencer ke taur par aapki zimmedariyan aur shartein." review={true} related={[{ href: '/hosts/rules', label: 'Influencer rules' }, { href: '/hosts/agreement', label: 'Influencer agreement' }]}>
<h2>Your role</h2><p>You work as an independent contractor. You are not an employee of {BRAND.name}. You choose your available hours and remain responsible for your conduct and statements.</p>
<h2>Payment and conduct</h2><p>Payment is calculated under <a href="/hosts/rates">rates, withdrawals &amp; taxes</a>. You must meet the <a href="/hosts/requirements">influencer requirements</a> and follow the <a href="/hosts/rules">influencer rules</a>. Nobody else may use your account to take calls.</p>
<h2>Safety</h2><p>No human monitors or listens to calls. Both numbers are masked, and pressing # ends the call and blocks the other person. See the <a href="/safety">safety centre</a>.</p>
<h2>Wellbeing duties</h2><p>You follow the <a href="/hosts/crisis-script">welfare &amp; crisis guide</a>. You give no medical, medicine, legal, money or relationship advice. You do not flirt, form a romantic relationship, share contact details or meet callers. You do not keep a distressed or attached caller on the line to earn more minutes, or encourage a caller to depend on you — doing so is a removal offence. You flag welfare and attachment concerns promptly so the platform can act.</p>
<h2>Suspension and termination</h2><p>Rule breaches can lead to a warning, suspension or removal. Serious safety concerns may require immediate action. Any withheld earnings will be reviewed individually under the published withdrawal terms and applicable law; a report alone does not forfeit earnings. You may stop taking calls and request account closure.</p>
<h2>Responsibility for your words</h2><p>To the extent allowed by law, you agree to cover the platform's losses and reasonable costs arising from your unlawful statements or your breach of these rules. This does not remove rights that the law gives you.</p>
<h2>Disputes</h2><p>Contact <a href="/grievance">the grievance contact</a> first. Both sides will try mediation before court proceedings. Indian law applies, subject to mandatory legal rights.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
